From 4e1fcc6193e385d4bc273d22894ad69a7bc6bb83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Coinupbtc <coinupbtc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:21:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: interleave decode rounds with a long prompt pass, and
 take cancels between its chunks (TF_DS_PREFILL_INTERLEAVE_MS)

A prompt pass ran whole inside its admission (LaneHost.admitOne), so every other live stream got no
decode round until it finished, and a cancel waited for it (issue #3 of the recipe). With
TF_DS_PREFILL_INTERLEAVE_MS=N (default unset: off, the engine unchanged), between two of a pass's
2,048-row chunks rank 0 runs the other live streams' rounds for up to N ms, delivers their tokens and
takes their cancels. The filling job is left alone: its own cancel stays in 'cancels' for its pass.

Safety: every state a pass carries from chunk to chunk is its slot's (window rings, raw stores,
compressed extent, drafter rings). The one shared piece, the Engram read-ahead (eh.hashes), is joined
before an interleaved round (and in Model.verify); fillChunk keeps the joined rows. Rank 1 needs no
protocol change: it runs the frames in order (fill_chunk re-arms its read-ahead after a verify frame).
Prompts with images run whole as before. Off when the core logs a trail (a step resets its arena).

Test: lane_host.zig, a decoding stream gets tokens during another's six-chunk pass and its cancel lands
before that pass ends (fake backend calls Stream.between between chunks).
---
